hey this is presh talwalkar  this problem from the scottish national  five maths exam  is getting a lot of attention because  students felt it was too difficult  chris has an umbrella that is 85  centimeters long  his locker is a cuboid with the length  40 centimeters width 40 centimeters and  height 70 centimeters  can the umbrella fit inside the locker  diagonally between corners p and m  which are opposite corners of the cuboid  i should mention this problem is  recreated from a not yet released exam  so while this may not be the exact  wording i've done my best to recreate  the problem based on posts to twitter  facebook and an article in the scottish  sun  can you figure it out  give this problem a try and when you're  ready keep watching the video for a  solution  one way to solve the problem is to use  the distance formula  imagine setting up a coordinate system  the point p can be placed at the origin  0 0 0.  the point m would then be at a  coordinate of 40 negative 40 and 70.  we can find the distance of pm by using  the distance formula  this becomes the square root of the  quantity 40 squared plus  the quantity negative 40 squared plus 70  squared  this simplifies to be the square root of  8100 which equals 90.  therefore the umbrella can fit because  the locker diagonal is 90 centimeters  which is larger than the umbrella which  is 85 centimeters  another way to solve this problem is to  use the pythagorean theorem twice  in the base square label point n  opposite the corner of p  this makes a right triangle with two  legs of 40. pn is the hypotenuse of this  right triangle so we can calculate the  length of pn as the square root of 40  squared plus 40 squared which equals 40  times the square root of 2.  we can then draw a triangle p and m  and that's another right triangle  this has legs of 40 square root of 2 and  70. so pm is the hypotenuse of this  right triangle and we can calculate its  distance by taking the square root  of the quantity 40 times the square root  of 2 squared plus  70 squared  this again simplifies to be the square  root of 8100 which is 90.  so once again we've calculated pm is 90.  so once again we could say the umbrella  can fit since the locker diagonal is 90  centimeters which is larger than the  umbrella which is 85 centimeters  did you figure it out and do you think  it was too difficult  thanks for watching this video please  subscribe to my channel i make videos on  math you can catch me on my blog mind  your decisions if you like this video  you can check out my books which are  listed in the video description and you  can support me on patreon if you have a  math topic you could email me presh  mindyourdecisions.com and you can catch  me on social media either at mind your  decisions or at preshtalwalkar
 

